{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:22:14.697958Z","id":"fc658f2c08c0f33b60daa58a70b1a3c3f59f6ae6d41edd6d3b92a9a72c6e4bfa","body":{"detail":"test/clax/http_api_test.dart checks the request (POST /api/artifacts/<aid>/versions:restore, body {version, if_version}, no X-Clax-Session) and the parsed answer. test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart does not call it, because the route (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs `restore`) was not on the branch when the client landed. The macOS integration test's Restore step, or a line in http_api_real_test.dart, should exercise it against the daemon, including a stale if_version (409 conflict with current).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":123},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"f91e24fb1030ae468367c885b24d59bc517d77bd7a1f66b7110f8086e2d20842"},"summary":"restoreVersion is tested only against the scripted server, not the real daemon","tags":["test-gap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:22:14.698043Z","id":"4720080d8cf2cee3bfbdfa71bf043182f17d07ad12f74f167a6d588df180ff09","body":{"detail":"The client and its scripted test follow the shape {collections: [{path, count}]} from docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 3.8. Until that route lands, the call answers 404 (ClaxApiError status 404), so a caller summarising other apps must treat a 404 as no collections. Once the route exists, add it to test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":260},"end":{"line":272},"content_hash":"e309b9cb1b965dea4c1ea8254e27257e056f30f4a2d277da37b6da2c55bdbe36"},"summary":"collections() calls GET docs:collections, a route the daemon does not have yet","tags":["test-gap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:22:14.698089Z","id":"835cbc19df61800aa57feab783aa1936d0ac0aac18f7bebe32d069cb39cfd127","body":{"detail":"POST /api/sessions/<sid>/feedback/ack accepts thread_ids or comment_ids (crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs AckBody); it has no feedback_ids field. The design's signature ackFeedback(sid, feedbackIds) is therefore ackFeedback(sid, commentIds): callers pass FeedbackItem.commentId. Acknowledging by comment rather than thread leaves a later comment on the same thread pending.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":57},"content_hash":"b3e9499425e3a21ea94f6edd19466f855f0e28d49b9fd9f462e7cee7f3a659da"},"summary":"ackFeedback takes comment IDs, not feedback IDs","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541171Z","id":"34bc319d1500749f5d3456c61057ca999de112775365ed5bb4688e0877358aa3","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/sessions/<sid>/working/<aid> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/working.rs:88-131) answers 404 not_found both for an unknown session (live(), line 19) and for an unknown artifact (st.get_artifact(&id)?.ok_or(CoreError::NotFound), line 107). setWorking wraps the call in _sessionCall (http_api.dart:393-407), which rewrites every 404 not_found to code unknown_session. An artifact the person deleted while its change was queued therefore looks like a lost session, and a worker that re-registers on unknown_session (spec 3.6) re-registers instead of dropping the change. Map 404 to unknown_session only on the routes whose sole resource is the session (pollFeedback, ackFeedback), and let setWorking's 404 stay not_found; FakeClaxApi.setWorking (fake_api.dart:403-404) already throws not_found for an unknown artifact, so the two disagree today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":228},"content_hash":"907b4ef775a05dfa43514008abf33d2499b9db163b6e16310bd71164d4556c5f"},"summary":"setWorking reports an unknown artifact as unknown_session","tags":["review","api-contract","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541323Z","id":"0f859815dfd4694c7d09cc8102f956207cb0cc44ed5f3cededac75af37f4b8d9","body":{"detail":"POST /api/artifacts/{aid}/versions:restore is routed (crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs api_slow) and implemented (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:692-754). test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart already has v1 (index.html + app.js) and v2 (app.js removed); a restoreVersion(aid, 1, ifVersion: 2) there can assert v3 with label 'Restored v1', readFiles(aid, 3) equal to v1's files, a stale ifVersion as 409 conflict with current, an unknown n as 404, and the documents written later untouched. A few lines close this record with evidence.","kind":"comment","references":"fc658f2c08c0f33b60daa58a70b1a3c3f59f6ae6d41edd6d3b92a9a72c6e4bfa","span":{"start":{"line":123},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"f91e24fb1030ae468367c885b24d59bc517d77bd7a1f66b7110f8086e2d20842"},"summary":"The restore route is in the daemon now; the real-daemon test should cover restoreVersion","tags":["review","test-gap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541476Z","id":"de290450a013a3c9370a437691c26f6c7ae7a2b48ddba3e316704fb8ec257977","body":{"detail":"The daemon checks X-Clax-Session on create and publish (publishing_session, crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:136-150) and answers 400 unknown_session when it names an ended or unknown session. FakeClaxApi.createArtifact and publish never call _liveSession, so after endSession(installId) they still succeed as the old session ID. F4b's worker must re-register on unknown_session (spec 3.6), and a test of that against the fake passes even when the loop never handles a refused publish. Check _liveSession(sessionId!) in createArtifact and publish when sessionId is set, as replyAsAgent/resolveAsAgent/setWorking already do.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":289},"content_hash":"ab4970d9c76a65c1a87522d0457681e6f64c19eb6870317946a57bac3dd14061"},"summary":"FakeClaxApi creates and publishes as an ended session; the daemon refuses with unknown_session","tags":["review","fake-fidelity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541518Z","id":"d7ac8febd7711785f1d1b8a92aed40d8c199dc52916c30070157764f74c7ad14","body":{"detail":"With sessionId null, _send omits X-Clax-Session (line 508) and the daemon creates an artifact with no owner session: no watch, so comments sent on it reach no app session and the worker never sees them. replyAsAgent, resolveAsAgent and setWorking refuse with StateError before any request (_needSession); createArtifact and publish, the other agent calls named in api.dart:10-12, could do the same. FakeClaxApi.createArtifact (fake_api.dart:241) also accepts a null session.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"c0c8c4da13087d58e88f58d18f7be4a4e341761c3298c9b539b33581795dc873"},"summary":"createArtifact and publish without a session silently act as the owner","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541568Z","id":"a72c87160b3c6cece93d6b41a17e63995696bf20a9c215920c7395daaebed0d4","body":{"detail":"getDoc treats every 404 as 'no document', but the daemon's missing-document 404 carries error.path (crates/clax-server/src/error.rs:46-50, DocNotFound) and a missing artifact's does not. clip (lines 230-239) likewise returns null for an unknown artifact or thread. FakeClaxApi.getDoc (fake_api.dart:490-494) and clip (412-418) throw not_found for those, so code tested against the fake meets a different answer in the app. Return null only for a 404 with body['path'] in getDoc, and align the fake with whichever rule is chosen.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":286},"end":{"line":295},"content_hash":"476246ba61a8b2773e2c8f4e1b5c8021cb36400581be52f0c844c6d02a7e0c80"},"summary":"getDoc and clip return null for an unknown artifact; the fake throws not_found","tags":["review","fake-fidelity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541613Z","id":"15f533322444ee4fcc43b475886f237b640aa3a4a6a36eb23ecf13853ebcdba8","body":{"detail":"The daemon's stream always starts with event ready {resumed} (crates/clax-server/src/routes/events.rs, the ready once-stream), and HttpClaxApi.events documents ready/resync as the listener's cue to refetch (api.dart:97-101). The fake's stream yields only what emit() sends, and its data omits the type field the daemon serialises. A screen (F8) that refetches on ready behaves differently against the fake. Emit ready {resumed: false} to each new listener.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":523},"end":{"line":531},"content_hash":"064d5624b07482ddea552f75febe33008ab59b9b23ecbc8ac35a7e487cd8836f"},"summary":"FakeClaxApi.events never opens with ready, unlike GET /api/events","tags":["review","fake-fidelity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/sse.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541660Z","id":"d37c76e8d9f1b90dad1c42a4ab791ef0605f575e011dabc9f72a3b7a55373ccc","body":{"detail":"The daemon sends a ': keep-alive' comment every 15 s while idle (crates/clax-server/src/daemon.rs sse_keep_alive). reconnectingSse waits on open() and on the connection with no limit, so a connection that stops delivering bytes without closing (a frozen daemon, a socket left half-open after the app is suspended) is never replaced. A deadline of a few keep-alive periods with no bytes, and a connect timeout on open, would turn that into an ordinary reconnect with Last-Event-ID.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":138},"content_hash":"431e780e8916a7bc577c1b2fe71ebe7105048d63ccf10c365618668be486add3"},"summary":"The event stream has no idle or connect deadline","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:33:52.333224Z","id":"33e40ddf60308168bdba2799e288ac6808206c672fe0100cc7e303093daef3d5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:191a54d9","summary":"Fixed: FakeClaxApi.createArtifact and publish check _liveSession(_needSession()). fake_api_test.dart 'create and publish need a live session' passes (unknown_session after endSession, StateError with none; flutter test test/clax: all passed).","supersedes":"de290450a013a3c9370a437691c26f6c7ae7a2b48ddba3e316704fb8ec257977","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:33:52.333458Z","id":"32269e70560f728a681ecc3468479871206de357ac16dc561cda4b8d680315ab","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:191a54d9","summary":"Fixed: FakeClaxApi.events gives each listener ready {resumed: false} first, lets ready and resync pass every filter, and its version data carries type, artifact_id, n, by_page and title as the daemon serialises. fake_api_test.dart 'events open with ready, then version events their filters keep' passes.","supersedes":"15f533322444ee4fcc43b475886f237b640aa3a4a6a36eb23ecf13853ebcdba8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:33:52.333617Z","id":"c28cb37caf5569f8d1c234a8db391a071ba372a4058a977cfa582b5dea6046de","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:191a54d9","summary":"Fixed: HttpClaxApi.createArtifact and publish call _needSession and throw StateError before any request without a session (publish checks ifVersion first). http_api_test.dart 'agent calls without a registered session are refused before any request' covers both and passes.","supersedes":"d7ac8febd7711785f1d1b8a92aed40d8c199dc52916c30070157764f74c7ad14","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:33:52.333779Z","id":"c98ecae0bcf0de37ffd9c5d0e873d13198d4a2e1c7b062dbb48eb0f1e366c72e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:191a54d9","summary":"Fixed: http_api_real_test.dart restores version 1 against the real daemon: version 3 labelled 'Restored v1' with v1's files, documents and capabilities unchanged, a stale if_version is 409 conflict with current 3, an unknown version is 404. CLAX_TEST_BIN=... flutter test test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart passes.","supersedes":"fc658f2c08c0f33b60daa58a70b1a3c3f59f6ae6d41edd6d3b92a9a72c6e4bfa","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:33:52.333938Z","id":"41e1f6b0e06049d8657bf163d4ff739b69eeb9502db3667c8cd4f8efc0596be6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:191a54d9","summary":"Fixed: setWorking no longer goes through _sessionCall, so a 404 stays not_found. test/clax/http_api_test.dart 'setWorking on an unknown artifact stays not_found' and fake_api_test.dart 'setWorking on an unknown artifact is not_found' pass (flutter test test/clax: +64, all passed with CLAX_TEST_BIN).","supersedes":"34bc319d1500749f5d3456c61057ca999de112775365ed5bb4688e0877358aa3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:33:52.334089Z","id":"42969584f21d63f8703586cbe7db5926867685bfb69454cdaff8228cabee0426","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:191a54d9","summary":"Fixed: getDoc returns null only for a 404 whose error names path and throws not_found otherwise; clip keeps null for every 404 (the daemon's clip 404 cannot tell no clip from an unknown thread or artifact), documented in api.dart, and FakeClaxApi.clip now answers null for those too. http_api_test.dart 'getDoc on an unknown artifact is not_found, not null', 'clip answers null for any 404' and fake_api_test.dart 'getDoc and clip on an unknown artifact answer as the daemon does' pass.","supersedes":"a72c87160b3c6cece93d6b41a17e63995696bf20a9c215920c7395daaebed0d4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/sse.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:33:52.334243Z","id":"c7b0c6adcbf812f45d81e2eea3ccf99eef568e4e8c13f44b45daa5b47abd6e8a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:191a54d9","summary":"Fixed: reconnectingSse takes connectTimeout (default 10 s; the request is aborted through SseAborter) and idleTimeout (default 45 s, three keep-alives; any byte, comments included, re-arms it), each failing the connection into the usual reconnect with Last-Event-ID. sse_test.dart 'an answer that does not come within the connect deadline is abandoned and retried' and 'a connection silent past the idle deadline is replaced, resuming from its last ID' pass, six runs in a row.","supersedes":"d37c76e8d9f1b90dad1c42a4ab791ef0605f575e011dabc9f72a3b7a55373ccc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:34:08.648556Z","id":"efc6a3079071cb8643cab79b3c9ecb0e5a52f390b982535ae8a61361ec069a76","body":{"detail":"pushFeedback sets each thread's feedback_state to acknowledged at once, while the daemon stamps acknowledged_at when take_feedback hands the row to a poll (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:321-328). A test that queues a comment before FeedbackWorker starts therefore sees the thread as stranded during the worker's start-up recovery and as pending in the poll, which the daemon never shows; apps/clax_app/test/agent/worker_test.dart queues only after the worker is idle on a poll. Moving the state change into pollFeedback's hand-over would match the daemon.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":148},"content_hash":"cd3382cca1d71bf04d5ed13b15795fcc0bbce89fa8c595db8a301624cb6582c3"},"summary":"FakeClaxApi marks feedback acknowledged when it is queued, not when a poll takes it","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:35:59.589757Z","id":"439f219e4a7287c2fb9918da5dd72668257c3f36bad0341d81ec7d87dc386f8c","body":{"detail":"take_feedback sets acknowledged_at in the same UPDATE that sets delivered_at, and only when q.tier.in_band() (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:513-525; Tier::Wait is in-band, crates/clax-core/src/feedback.rs:644). Until a poll takes it, GET /api/threads shows feedback_state.state 'sent', which ThreadView.stranded (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/models.dart) excludes. FakeClaxApi.pushFeedback (fake_api.dart:140-143) sets 'acknowledged' when the batch is queued, so a batch queued before any poll reads as stranded and as pending at once. Set the state when pollFeedback hands the batch over (fake_api.dart:355-356, and when a waiting poll is completed at line 145), not when it is queued.","kind":"comment","references":"efc6a3079071cb8643cab79b3c9ecb0e5a52f390b982535ae8a61361ec069a76","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":149},"content_hash":"ab41689fbb9685d754cf837a7cc33d3560a5330bfed5cc2a3b24c0fd4f01d4cd"},"summary":"Confirmed: the daemon stamps acknowledged_at only when a wait-tier poll takes the row","tags":["review","fake-fidelity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/sse.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:35:59.589877Z","id":"70ffa398eead8de8d959f3da8f2917f2a427d13817ac3475ce440e563e2296c8","body":{"detail":"HttpClaxApi.events sets abort.onAbort only after _client.openUrl resolves (http_api.dart:374). SseAborter.abort called before that (the connect deadline firing, or a cancel, while the TCP connect is still pending) finds onAbort null and does nothing, so the request is still sent. Its answer then reaches _discard (the timeout path's pending.then(_discard), and the cancelled path at sse.dart:140-141), and _discard drains the response (sse.dart:234): for a 200 text/event-stream that never ends, so one connection stays open until the daemon shuts down, and on the cancelled path run() never returns. On loopback the window is small. SseAborter could remember an abort requested early and call onAbort as soon as it is set; _discard of a 200 could cancel the response's subscription (or detachSocket and destroy) instead of draining.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":68},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"52f7dd94ec911598ad84a1cf0d1a48fe3177da7aefe339d87d39906091f46f24"},"summary":"An abort requested before open() registers its handler is lost, and a discarded 200 event stream is drained forever","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:20.168142Z","id":"0ad2f3802da40481797707b3b9def3d343ea8e85767cfc4ac128675e72dc30ba","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fc541061","summary":"Fixed: pushFeedback no longer touches feedback_state; FakeClaxApi._handOver sets 'acknowledged' when pollFeedback takes a queued batch or pushFeedback completes a waiting poll, so a queued thread reads 'sent' and is not stranded until then. test/clax/fake_api_test.dart 'feedback reads sent until a poll takes it, then acknowledged' failed before and passes now; flutter test test/agent (F4b's worker and loop tests) still passes, +130.","supersedes":"efc6a3079071cb8643cab79b3c9ecb0e5a52f390b982535ae8a61361ec069a76","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/sse.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:20.168694Z","id":"6559beb4b5866f5ccefbbdea09233e5513a2d5eb93098f7e21d98e8d1b87fb18","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fc541061","summary":"Fixed: SseAborter remembers an abort asked for before onAbort is set and applies it when it is set; an answer arriving after a cancel or a missed connect deadline is closed by cancelling its subscription (_close) instead of drained. test/clax/sse_test.dart 'a stream cancelled while its answer is on the way closes that answer' hung to its timeout with the drain and passes now, as do the two SseAborter tests.","supersedes":"70ffa398eead8de8d959f3da8f2917f2a427d13817ac3475ce440e563e2296c8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:27:45.554252Z","id":"66a5f0ec7b17865a613241147d65d788d1c8ef47590fc60ab6130494891b4614","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"4720080d8cf2cee3bfbdfa71bf043182f17d07ad12f74f167a6d588df180ff09","summary":"The route now exists: GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/docs:collections (token) answers {collections: [{path, count}]} sorted by path, without private data/users/<id>/ collections (crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs collections, tested by crates/clax-server/tests/api_db_read.rs collections_lists_paths_and_counts, commit 53631fe2). It answers 401 without the token, 404 for an unknown artifact, and 403 not_granted with X-Clax-Reader. The 404 fallback this record describes is no longer needed; adding the call to test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart is left to the client's owner.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:42:33.972204Z","id":"3e8284bf907611a6d5ab113ae34d243f6d45b4e2450aa6f396d18ab5543fae55","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:53631fe2","summary":"The route exists (crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs, commit 53631fe2; reply 66a5f0ec). Against a scratch daemon (clax 5853b430, CLAX_HOME under target/, port 54089) with docs in runs (2) and boards/b1/columns (1): GET /api/artifacts/2h2gy81y5mp8/docs:collections with the Bearer token answered HTTP 200 {\"collections\":[{\"count\":1,\"path\":\"boards/b1/columns\"},{\"count\":2,\"path\":\"runs\"}]}, the shape collections() in apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart parses; without the token, HTTP 401. A 404 no longer stands for a missing route.","supersedes":"4720080d8cf2cee3bfbdfa71bf043182f17d07ad12f74f167a6d588df180ff09","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:47:47.096324Z","id":"de8f9dd108f746a5d8d442be05de9729a296c2fc8971296f4b6492953045de26","body":{"detail":"The body follows the POST /api/drafts interface of task S1 in docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2.md (Task S1, Interfaces), written before the route existed. POST /api/artifacts/<aid>/versions takes {path: {content}}; if crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs lands with that shape, or with deny_unknown_fields refusing null, every render's first push fails. The real-daemon check is apps/clax_app/test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart 'drafts: a hidden copy of the app that takes publishes and is deleted' (lines 387-458), skipped with a reason until the route exists: remove the skip and run it with CLAX_TEST_BIN once S1 is in.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":428},"end":{"line":446},"content_hash":"e1bbc6db911d82ecf8ec52c86215abcedf43168b7434175d6374aef971095e83"},"summary":"createDraft sends files as {path: text}, not the publish route's {path: {content}}, and of/capabilities as explicit nulls; unverified against a daemon","tags":["C1","S1","risk","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:47:47.096459Z","id":"0a23a623ad0e23924563a6b80e4051191f5d2b09bafb6dbe83b097e048c9a3ee","body":{"detail":"On POST /api/sessions/<sid>/questions, GET .../questions/<qid> and .../withdraw a 404 means an unknown session, an unknown or another session's question, or (create) an artifact_id that names no live artifact (crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs live(), create). The client cannot tell them apart, so it passes not_found through; an ended session is 400 unknown_session either way. The ask_owner tool must treat not_found on a wait or withdraw as 'the question or session is gone', and re-register the session only on unknown_session or a failing feedback poll.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":556},"end":{"line":599},"content_hash":"102703b58288c330d16162173c921bbe136e4260fc1290b99cf1bd922d83f1fb"},"summary":"The question session routes keep the daemon's 404 not_found for an unknown session: it is not mapped to unknown_session as pollFeedback's is","tags":["C1","A6","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:47:47.096560Z","id":"80e9d5e1a46c22db700618a406e992fc60faf6d16119e50593c7c56b3e923793","body":{"detail":"The daemon makes reply, version, published and finished items in the transaction of their source (docs/contract.md, The inbox, Items). The fake's replyAsAgent, publish, createArtifact and setWorking leave the inbox alone; tests add those items with pushInbox (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart, pushInbox). A widget test of the inbox (task N1) that expects an agent reply to appear there by itself must seed it, or the fake must grow the rules.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1207},"end":{"line":1246},"content_hash":"24f674d6576932193bc1f40c1b16ad6af9bbc99ff533ba1ac799145cb4a169bb"},"summary":"FakeClaxApi makes inbox items only for questions: agent replies, versions, creates and finished work make none, unlike the daemon","tags":["C1","N1","test-fidelity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:31:09.528037Z","id":"eec57641852aeaca940c3f0dea06c8cfbe9da3f6e4ff6411953161414fd7aeee","body":{"detail":"POST /api/sessions/<sid>/questions answers {question, mode, terminal_after_s, surface_open} (crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create). docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md R§8 (lines 465-470, 505-508) has the in-app ask tool return Clax's ask result including surface_open, and tell the agent not to wait when it is false; crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs ask_result reads it from this answer. With the current signature the Toolbox cannot report it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":179},"end":{"line":190},"content_hash":"eecd7c58c0f7cbdae436cdf61793da25655801865714bf407dc2c7e3510f9909"},"suggested_fix":"Return an AskResult {question, surfaceOpen, mode, terminalAfterS} (or add the fields) from askQuestion in api.dart, http_api.dart:557 and fake_api.dart:970, the fake taking surfaceOpen from whether one of its streams holds questions or inbox.","summary":"askQuestion returns only the question view and drops the create answer's surface_open, mode and terminal_after_s, which the agent's ask result needs","tags":["review","C1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:31:09.528221Z","id":"02945d038c7fb12b8ef294fc4b73f7898fe7c59817f59e0eb555cdc3b1b96f29","body":{"detail":"GET /api/sessions/<sid>/questions/<qid>?wait=0 answers at once with the open view (crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs poll; http_api_real_test.dart asserts it). In the fake the same call hangs, so a test of the ask tool's open/call_again path or a zero-wait recheck (clax-mcp tools.rs calls ask_wait(qid, 0)) never completes unless the test knows to call releaseQuestionWaits.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1041},"end":{"line":1057},"content_hash":"0990263c9cc812d6cf51009185d67af5932451c4f220e6676cb438e6c408a94a"},"suggested_fix":"Answer the open view at once when wait is zero; keep releaseQuestionWaits for longer waits.","summary":"FakeClaxApi.waitQuestion ignores wait: wait zero (or any wait running out) never answers open, it waits for a close or releaseQuestionWaits","tags":["review","C1","fake-fidelity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:31:09.528285Z","id":"8df872875b411048b9fbec8db76cff1bf0b1806f27f5400bc5820d76c278aaf1","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/questions.rs validate_answers refuses (400 invalid_answer) a label not among the options, a label twice, selections on a free-text question or one with no text, Other text when other is false, nothing picked, and two picks on a single-select question; Answer.selected is a Vec, so an explicit null is a 400 body error. models.dart QuestionAnswer.toJson (line 730) writes selected: null for a text-only answer, which the daemon refuses and the fake accepts. Fake question views then carry selected: null where the daemon's carry [].","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1088},"end":{"line":1106},"content_hash":"98ad3b7f45dd017d79a519189bf9c38dc64811441a5f720146ae2999fb22167d"},"suggested_fix":"Mirror validate_answers in the fake and normalise selected to []; make QuestionAnswer.toJson omit or empty a null selected.","summary":"FakeClaxApi.answerQuestion checks only the answer count and stores selected as given (null too); the daemon validates every answer and always returns a list","tags":["review","C1","fake-fidelity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:31:09.528345Z","id":"08c8041a916dfca71e034872d38c308cca5f129824e045e4c6d78c683244ae77","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/questions.rs Question and QOption are deny_unknown_fields (multiSelect instead of multi_select is 400 invalid_question) and limit description to 500 and preview to 20,000 characters; the daemon also answers 429 limit_reached past the open-question limits. The fake takes all of these.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1174},"end":{"line":1206},"content_hash":"bba0e32f3162b47390cbf458a2f894b33e29fc47975805f1e6eb305d3c3136fb"},"summary":"The fake's question validation accepts unknown keys and skips description and preview limits that the daemon enforces","tags":["review","C1","fake-fidelity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/stream.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:31:09.528387Z","id":"3526656829d2da4461bc98f507390710664f1b0277bbe72eff6b78ba4fcf4d4a","body":{"detail":"In _restoreEach a status 0 or 5xx leaves the topic in _wanted and out of _held and sends no resync for it; the next restore runs only on the next ready. Until the connection drops, the caller gets no events for that topic and no sign of it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":275},"end":{"line":301},"content_hash":"b5bd08ca816e10aea5d4148c832eb1f52902c210c054d477b2de3ec71744b5d2"},"suggested_fix":"Retry the transient ones with the same backoff as _restore, or emit resync/unsubscribed so the caller knows.","summary":"A topic whose single re-subscribe fails transiently stays wanted but unsubscribed, with no event and no retry while the connection stays up","tags":["review","C1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:31:15.846462Z","id":"5264bbb4047341c6b7856877d2a6c2681b39b35b9ba8465b78a72dbe941e4955","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"de8f9dd108f746a5d8d442be05de9729a296c2fc8971296f4b6492953045de26","summary":"Verified against the committed draft route: crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs CreateBody takes files as strings (DraftFile::Text, untagged) and of/capabilities as Option, so explicit nulls are None. The drafts test in test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart, unskipped and without its invalid data/users seed write, passes against a debug clax built from this branch (3 passed). Closable once the test is unskipped (record 67b9f757).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:12:07.363691Z","id":"57e20ba965f2bd5df55de9bbbe1247bec41f64a3fa3818133b8fb40ada4146db","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b29720d8","summary":"askQuestion returns AskResult {question, mode, terminalAfterS, surfaceOpen} from the create answer (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/models.dart AskResult). Tests: http_api_test.dart 'askQuestion creates an ask question for the session' and '... leaves artifact_id out' assert mode/terminal_after_s/surface_open; http_api_real_test.dart asserts ('wait', true) with a stream holding inbox and questions; fake_api_test.dart 'ask answers the create response...' asserts surfaceOpen false, then true once a fake stream holds questions. Evidence: flutter test test/clax: 134 passed, 3 skipped (the real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN); CLAX_TEST_BIN=<debug clax built from this branch> flutter test test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart: 3 passed.","supersedes":"eec57641852aeaca940c3f0dea06c8cfbe9da3f6e4ff6411953161414fd7aeee","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:12:07.365963Z","id":"27fd092339638b97ba09fca53cd90c609871d83fb6804052cede3b95b61228d7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b29720d8","summary":"FakeClaxApi.waitQuestion returns the open view at once for a zero wait, and otherwise when its wait runs out, on an injectable timer (FakeClaxApi(timer:)); a close cancels the timer. Tests: fake_api_test.dart 'a zero wait answers at once with the open view' and 'a wait that runs out answers the open view' (the later answer then arrives as a late answer). Evidence: flutter test test/clax: 134 passed, 3 skipped (the real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN); CLAX_TEST_BIN=<debug clax built from this branch> flutter test test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart: 3 passed.","supersedes":"02945d038c7fb12b8ef294fc4b73f7898fe7c59817f59e0eb555cdc3b1b96f29","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:12:07.367373Z","id":"5a2d98d16384783c76cae1cacd7a8d0b724617aa0285c816fe2602ead231eb83","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b29720d8","summary":"The fake's answerQuestion applies validate_answers' rules (unknown label, a label twice, two picks on single-select, blank or long text, picks on free text, Other text when other is false, nothing picked) and refuses selected: null or an unknown key as invalid_json; stored answers have selected as a list and text trimmed. QuestionAnswer.selected is now a non-null list and toJson writes [] for none. Tests: fake_api_test.dart 'answers follow the daemon rules'; http_api_test.dart 'question answers' group and the answerQuestion test, which posts QuestionAnswer(text: ...).toJson() as {selected: [], text}. Evidence: flutter test test/clax: 134 passed, 3 skipped (the real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN); CLAX_TEST_BIN=<debug clax built from this branch> flutter test test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart: 3 passed.","supersedes":"8df872875b411048b9fbec8db76cff1bf0b1806f27f5400bc5820d76c278aaf1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:12:07.368735Z","id":"db1dadc4926b835a82d6bd02eba446a0713a20633a9f0cd36d6fc00b0455f0d0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b29720d8","summary":"The fake's question validation refuses unknown question and option keys, blank (spaces only) text, description over 500 and preview over 20,000 characters, multi_select without options and two recommended options, and askQuestion answers 429 limit_reached at 8 open questions per session or 100 in all. Test: fake_api_test.dart 'questions follow the daemon rules and limits'. Evidence: flutter test test/clax: 134 passed, 3 skipped (the real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN); CLAX_TEST_BIN=<debug clax built from this branch> flutter test test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart: 3 passed.","supersedes":"08c8041a916dfca71e034872d38c308cca5f129824e045e4c6d78c683244ae77","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/stream.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:12:07.370099Z","id":"02c1e76fa4ae0eeab969339c186e2026c530741c0367dd72b99376dd6be01edc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b29720d8","summary":"SseClaxStream._restore retries a re-subscription that fails with status 0 or 5xx, of all topics or of one alone, with backoff for SseClaxStream.restoreAttempts (6) tries, then drops those topics with an unsubscribed event carrying the last error code. Tests: stream_test.dart 'a re-subscribe that fails for a while is retried until it holds', 'a topic whose single re-subscribe fails for a while is retried alone', 'a re-subscribe that keeps failing gives up with unsubscribed per topic'. Evidence: flutter test test/clax: 134 passed, 3 skipped (the real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN); CLAX_TEST_BIN=<debug clax built from this branch> flutter test test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart: 3 passed.","supersedes":"3526656829d2da4461bc98f507390710664f1b0277bbe72eff6b78ba4fcf4d4a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:12:07.372772Z","id":"07f7a334d9816dd5941be84d00df4184a14b18baa12ddf66ef14294955db0b48","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b29720d8","summary":"Verified against the daemon's draft routes: crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs takes each file as a string (or a publish's object) and of/capabilities as optional, so createDraft's body is accepted; http_api_real_test.dart 'drafts: a hidden copy of the app that takes publishes and is deleted' creates, lists, publishes to, writes to and deletes a draft. Evidence: flutter test test/clax: 134 passed, 3 skipped (the real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN); CLAX_TEST_BIN=<debug clax built from this branch> flutter test test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart: 3 passed.","supersedes":"de8f9dd108f746a5d8d442be05de9729a296c2fc8971296f4b6492953045de26","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:33:36.234529Z","id":"85bff3884b2d98e4644722fc8978601acf9ba2cb96f48a2eefcb119f03dafad4","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs:261-269 refuses a request whose files map lacks index.html (missing_index), whatever the previous version held. The fake (here and publish at lines 406-416) carries the previous files forward first and checks after, which hid the render tool's incremental-publish defect (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart:224-256). finish's publish (A3) can hit the same gap.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":776},"end":{"line":800},"content_hash":"025222f2e610d3d370373cddecbab8c0db84ef64ec054a077707a66d478e51a3"},"suggested_fix":"Check r.files['index.html'] != null before merging, as the daemon does.","summary":"FakeClaxApi.publishDraft and publish check index.html in the merged file set, but the daemon requires index.html in every publish request, so tests pass for publishes the daemon refuses","tags":["review","review:A5","fake","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:47.157123Z","id":"fa8abfd44e8eb3d76a562db4b15b4ecf57726a3283bbf576c22f2073e66acd25","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8fe9730a","summary":"FakeClaxApi.publish and publishDraft now refuse a request whose files lack index.html (missing_index, _needIndex), as crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs does. Evidence: with this fake, the render tool's old incremental publish fails the unit tests 'a removed file…', 'a change to app.js alone…' and 'a title-only change…' (seen red before b290498a); version_page_test.dart's publishes now name index.html and pass (14/14); the full flutter test run shows no missing_index failure.","supersedes":"85bff3884b2d98e4644722fc8978601acf9ba2cb96f48a2eefcb119f03dafad4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:56:08.652101Z","id":"3e4abf1810184fd293236cd4ace3920872f55fe3350a8b5ec929fb1ae216a879","body":{"detail":"The daemon refuses a published path that is empty, absolute, has a . or .. segment, a backslash or a control character, two paths that differ only by case, a file over 16 MiB and files over 64 MiB together (docs/contract.md, publish errors). _requestFiles and its callers accept all of them, so a bundle install or update test on the fake cannot see those refusals.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1852},"end":{"line":1859},"content_hash":"36952f5392713d612de9a4546cb4b50659ee46fa68cae72ce4e86d1b785d8041"},"suggested_fix":"Validate paths and sizes in _requestFiles when a test needs those refusals.","summary":"FakeClaxApi takes any file path and size: it never answers invalid_path, file_too_large or body_too_large as the daemon does","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:59:18.409433Z","id":"9cd8eae2b0d4bbcfa4640e84304aa179ff9813bd65adf063d593828206ca9a1a","body":{"detail":"A FileEntry without a type takes _type(path). The daemon resolves it with content_type_for: js/mjs as text/javascript, everything else by mime_guess, no charset. Since d9f7ebbd the fake stores and reports that type in FileMeta.contentType, so an exporter test on the fake writes types into a manifest that a real daemon would never report. The content hash ignores types, so no hash check is affected.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1928},"end":{"line":1938},"content_hash":"76a1b3f290a119d050928720b8340b6274be78280cca59a2f8bc9877ece1ce8b"},"suggested_fix":"Match content_type_for for the extensions a bundle carries (html, css, js, json, svg, png, md, csv, txt), or note in the class doc that types differ.","summary":"FakeClaxApi's default content types differ from the daemon's: text/html; charset=utf-8 where crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs content_type_for (mime_guess) gives text/html, and text/plain for .md and .csv","tags":["review","review:BA","fake","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:59:18.465603Z","id":"57ea5d071388f4b29278dd80fe56d4fd763e307487f9c50aa89b5d8c66c8ddb6","body":{"detail":"_FakeFile holds the bytes it was given and computes sha256 once; readFileBytes hands that same buffer out. HttpClaxApi always returns a fresh buffer. A test that reuses or zeroes a buffer would see the fake diverge from the daemon silently.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":462},"end":{"line":466},"content_hash":"4961cf259d1d62fdf65d409d730c72d0b01d41dc85c4cd746a5ef9fd7f934057"},"suggested_fix":"Uint8List.fromList on store and on read.","summary":"FakeClaxApi.readFileBytes returns the stored Uint8List itself, and a FileEntry.bytes buffer is kept by reference: a caller that writes into either changes the fake's stored version while its cached sha256 stays","tags":["review","review:BA","fake","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
